# Main fsm in adamsbridge_ctrl module never checks if the last msg is sent or dropped in message interface.

- Source URL: https://github.com/chipsalliance/adams-bridge/issues/78

The msg interface driven by the adamsbridge_ctrl has a valid(msg_valid_o) and ready(msg_rdy_i). The valid signal is asserted when the message is being loaded to the keccak buffer for the length defined by the sequencer. And this interface is flopped by a clk cycle. Now once the last msg which is set(msg_done and there is no hold) the fsm in the ctrl module makes a transition from  `MLDSA_CTRL_MSG_LOAD to   `MLDSA_CTRL_FUNC_START with  valid and valid data but if there is no ready signal incoming from the present clk cycle then the valid stays asserted till the ready is asserted. But the main fsm never checks if this last msg is ever sent to the keccak and advances in the transitions.

